const e="mumbai-university-youth-festival",h=2024,t="Read the whole 27-page circular (eligibility rules p.1-2, event rules p.3-27). It prints no dates, venue or address, entry fee, contact person or number, prizes, points or grades, no steps for how an institution registers, and no rule for the Zonal/District level except the two round names. It gives the template's single age group no separate rule: the eligibility is for every student. The template titles ending '(Any Other Language)' are the circular's Group B (Hindi or English) for Elocution, Debate, Story Writing and Story Telling, and Group C (other than Marathi) for Mono Acting, One Act Play and Skit; the base titles are Group A (Marathi). The circular calls Indian Classical Dance an 'Individual Event' and the other single-person music items 'Solo Event'. The circular states ages and dates for the 57th festival (2024-25); they are kept as Variables as a starting suggestion for the next edition.",n={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"University of Mumbai Youth Festival, 57th edition (Academic Year 2024-25). Read the eligibility rules before you send a team.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Only a bonafide full-time student of an Affiliated College, Constituent College, Recognized Institute, Centre or Academic Department of the University of Mumbai can take part, and only for the institution where he or she studies. The student must be under 25 years of age on {{AgeCutoffDate}}.",Notes:["Organiser: {{Organiser}}. Edition: {{FestivalEdition}}.","Each institution sends one entry in each competition: one student in a solo or individual event, and one team in a group event.","Papers, scripts and notes for an event are handed in at registration on the day of the competition. Each event says how many copies to bring.","The rules in this circular print no dates, venue, entry fee, contact person, prizes or points."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["The festival is the {{FestivalEdition}}. It is organised by the {{Organiser}}.","The event rules are in five sections: Music, Dance, Literary, Theatre and Fine Art. Short Film Making and Jackpot are two more events outside these sections.","Many Literary and Theatre events have a Marathi version (Group A) and a second version (Group B in Hindi or English, or Group C in any Indian regional or official language other than Marathi).","A performance is timed from the organisers' final announcement, unless the event rule gives another starting point."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who Can Enter",Items:["A bonafide, full-time student can take part if he or she is enrolled under the University of Mumbai in a Degree Programme, a Post-graduate Degree Programme, or a Diploma Programme of at least one academic year whose examination the University conducts after the 12th class examination.","Students enrolled in a correspondence course at an Affiliated College, Constituent College, Recognized Institute, Centre or Academic Department of the University of Mumbai are not eligible.","Casual students, external students and students doing only a bridge course are not eligible.","A student enrolled in a distance education programme of the University is not eligible.","A student with provisional admission is not eligible.","A student can represent only the Affiliated College, Constituent College, Recognized Institute, Centre or Academic Department where he or she is studying for the degree or diploma.","The student must have a valid PRN No. or Registration No., an Identity Card and a Fees Receipt of the institution where he or she is studying.","A student who migrates from another University can take part only when the admission is regularised and he or she is admitted as a bonafide student.","A student employed full time is not eligible.","A student cannot represent more than one institution during the Youth Festival.","Not more than 7 years may have passed since the student passed the examination that qualified him or her for first admission to a degree or diploma course.","The student must be less than 25 years of age on {{AgeCutoffDate}}.","A student can take part for one year more than the normal length of the course. A student in a three-year degree (such as B.A., B.Sc., B.Com.) can take part for four years. A student in a four-year programme (such as B.E., B.Tech.) can take part for five years.","To count the years of eligibility, one year means the academic year in which the Youth Festival is held, whether or not the student's result is declared. It normally runs from June or July of one year for 12 calendar months to the next year."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"Registration",Items:["The papers an event needs (scripts, song texts with their meaning, notes, character lists) are handed in at registration on the day of the competition. Each event says what to bring and how many copies.","Where an event asks for a text in Marathi or English, the text can be written in Marathi or English as that event says."]},{Key:"teams",Title:"Entries from One Institution",Items:["Each participating College, Institute or University Academic Department sends only 1 student in a solo or individual event.","Each participating College, Institute or University Academic Department sends a single team in a group event. The team size is printed under each event."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Rounds",Items:["The rules name a Zonal/District Level Cultural Youth Festival (Selection Round) and a University Level Cultural Youth Festival (Final Round). Quiz and Indian Classical Dance say what is different in each round."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Disqualification for Breaking the Eligibility Rules",Items:["A participant disqualified because he or she is not eligible is scratched from the Youth Festival automatically.","A participant disqualified because he or she is not eligible cannot take part in the next Youth Festival (printed as the 58th)."]}],Documents:[{Title:"Rules and Regulations of the 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 (PDF)",Url:"https://unimumbaidsd.com/2024-25/docs/Circular-Rules-YF-2024-25.pdf"}]},i=[],o=[],a=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Indian Classical Vocal Solo","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item i, p.3","Sections":{"About":["Solo event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["The item is presented in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.","Up to 2 accompanists."],"Allowed":["The student may use an instrument such as Tanpura, Electronic Tanpura or Swarmandal."],"NotAllowed":["Film songs."],"Judging":["Selection of raga, presentation and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the details of Raag, Taal and Bandish, written in Marathi or English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The item is presented in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.\\n- Up to 2 accompanists.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The student may use an instrument such as Tanpura, Electronic Tanpura or Swarmandal.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Selection of raga, presentation and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the details of Raag, Taal and Bandish, written in Marathi or English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Indian Classical Instrumental Percussion Solo","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item ii (Taalvadya), p.3","Sections":{"About":["Solo event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement. Participants should tune their instruments well before.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["The item is presented in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.","Only 1 accompanist.","The participant brings his or her own instruments."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Selection of taal, presentation and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement. Participants should tune their instruments well before.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The item is presented in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.\\n- Only 1 accompanist.\\n- The participant brings his or her own instruments.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Selection of taal, presentation and general impression."},{"Title":"Indian Classical Instrumental Non-Percussion Solo","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item iii (Swarvadya), p.4","Sections":{"About":["Solo event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement. Participants should tune their instruments well before.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["The item is presented in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.","Only 1 accompanist.","The participant brings his or her own instruments."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Swar, taal, selection of raga and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement. Participants should tune their instruments well before.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The item is presented in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.\\n- Only 1 accompanist.\\n- The participant brings his or her own instruments.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Swar, taal, selection of raga and general impression."},{"Title":"Natyasangeet Vocal Solo","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item iv, p.4","Sections":{"About":["Solo event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["The student presents a song or natyapad (a song from musical theatre) from any theatre section of India.","The song or natyapad must be of natyageet style. Any other type of song (ovi or bhavgeet) is not counted as natyageet.","Up to 2 accompanists. The student may also play an instrument."],"Allowed":["A natyapad from a film song.","The student and the accompanists may use an instrument such as Tanpura, Electronic Tanpura or Swarmandal."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Sur, taal and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in Marathi or English (for songs in a language other than Marathi or Hindi), are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student presents a song or natyapad (a song from musical theatre) from any theatre section of India.\\n- The song or natyapad must be of natyageet style. Any other type of song (ovi or bhavgeet) is not counted as natyageet.\\n- Up to 2 accompanists. The student may also play an instrument.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- A natyapad from a film song.\\n- The student and the accompanists may use an instrument such as Tanpura, Electronic Tanpura or Swarmandal.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Sur, taal and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in Marathi or English (for songs in a language other than Marathi or Hindi), are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Indian Light Vocal Solo","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item v, p.5","Sections":{"About":["Solo event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 4 to 6 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["The songs are in any regional or official language of India, other than English.","Up to 2 accompanists. The student may also play an instrument."],"Allowed":["The student and the accompanists may use a synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget."],"NotAllowed":["Film songs."],"Judging":["Swara, taal and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in Marathi or English (for songs in a language other than Marathi or Hindi), are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 4 to 6 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The songs are in any regional or official language of India, other than English.\\n- Up to 2 accompanists. The student may also play an instrument.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The student and the accompanists may use a synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Swara, taal and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in Marathi or English (for songs in a language other than Marathi or Hindi), are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Indian Group Song","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item vi, p.5","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Total performance for both songs: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 5 minutes at most."],"Rules":["A single team of 4 to 6 students.","The team sings two songs: one patriotic song and one Indian folk song.","The songs are in any regional or official language of India, other than English.","Up to 3 accompanists. Student participants may play instruments while singing."],"Allowed":["A synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget, used in one mode only."],"NotAllowed":["Film songs."],"Judging":["Composition, choice of songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. Make-up, costumes and actions of the team are not judged."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in Marathi or English (for songs in a language other than Marathi or Hindi), are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Total performance for both songs: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 4 to 6 students.\\n- The team sings two songs: one patriotic song and one Indian folk song.\\n- The songs are in any regional or official language of India, other than English.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists. Student participants may play instruments while singing.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- A synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget, used in one mode only.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Composition, choice of songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. Make-up, costumes and actions of the team are not judged.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in Marathi or English (for songs in a language other than Marathi or Hindi), are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Folk Orchestra","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item vii, p.6","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 8 to 10 minutes, not counting the time to set up and tune the instruments. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Setting and tuning of instruments: 10 minutes at most."],"Rules":["A single team of 6 to 9 students.","The team plays original folk tunes of Maharashtra. The instruments must be original for that folk tune and suited to folk art of Maharashtra.","Up to 3 accompanists. They wear a different dress from the student participants so that they can be seen easily as accompanists.","The accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants and do not lead the team."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Folk tunes played in films."],"Judging":["Originality, composition, synchronization and variety. Make-up, costumes and actions of the team are not judged."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 8 to 10 minutes, not counting the time to set up and tune the instruments. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Setting and tuning of instruments: 10 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 6 to 9 students.\\n- The team plays original folk tunes of Maharashtra. The instruments must be original for that folk tune and suited to folk art of Maharashtra.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists. They wear a different dress from the student participants so that they can be seen easily as accompanists.\\n- The accompanists sit or stand separately from the participants and do not lead the team.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Folk tunes played in films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Originality, composition, synchronization and variety. Make-up, costumes and actions of the team are not judged."},{"Title":"Qawwali","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item viii, p.6","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Total performance for both Qawwali songs: 12 to 15 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 10 minutes at most."],"Rules":["A single team of 6 to 10 students (male, female or both).","The team sings two Qawwali songs: one on the theme National Integration and one on the theme Communal Harmony.","Up to 3 accompanists. Student participants may play instruments while singing.","The team brings its own musical instruments."],"Allowed":["Film songs.","A synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget, used in one mode only."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Composition, choice of Qawwali songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. Make-up, costumes and actions of the team are not judged."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the Qawwali songs with their meaning, written in Marathi or English (for songs in a language other than Marathi or Hindi), are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Total performance for both Qawwali songs: 12 to 15 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 10 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 6 to 10 students (male, female or both).\\n- The team sings two Qawwali songs: one on the theme National Integration and one on the theme Communal Harmony.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists. Student participants may play instruments while singing.\\n- The team brings its own musical instruments.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n- A synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget, used in one mode only.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Composition, choice of Qawwali songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. Make-up, costumes and actions of the team are not judged.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the Qawwali songs with their meaning, written in Marathi or English (for songs in a language other than Marathi or Hindi), are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Western Vocal Solo","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item ix, p.7","Sections":{"About":["Solo event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance for all songs: 4 to 6 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["The songs are in English only.","The student may sing any number of songs.","Up to 2 accompanists. The student may also play an instrument."],"Allowed":["Film songs.","The student and the accompanists may use a synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Selection of songs, pitch, rhythm and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance for all songs: 4 to 6 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The songs are in English only.\\n- The student may sing any number of songs.\\n- Up to 2 accompanists. The student may also play an instrument.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n- The student and the accompanists may use a synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Selection of songs, pitch, rhythm and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Western Instrumental Solo","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item x, p.7","Sections":{"About":["Solo event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["The student plays western music on any western percussion or non-percussion instrument.","The student performs one genre or style of western music, or fuses several genres or styles.","Up to 2 accompanists."],"Allowed":["The accompanists may use a synthesizer or any other electronic instrument."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Rhythm, harmony and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student plays western music on any western percussion or non-percussion instrument.\\n- The student performs one genre or style of western music, or fuses several genres or styles.\\n- Up to 2 accompanists.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The accompanists may use a synthesizer or any other electronic instrument.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Rhythm, harmony and general impression."},{"Title":"Western Group Song","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Music Section item xi, p.8","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Total performance for all songs: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 5 minutes at most."],"Rules":["A single team of 4 to 6 students.","The songs are in English only.","The team may sing any number of songs.","Up to 3 accompanists. Student participants may play western instruments while singing."],"Allowed":["Film songs.","A synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Composition, choice of songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. Make-up, costumes and actions of the team are not judged."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Total performance for all songs: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 4 to 6 students.\\n- The songs are in English only.\\n- The team may sing any number of songs.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists. Student participants may play western instruments while singing.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n- A synthesizer or any other electronic instrument or gadget.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Composition, choice of songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. Make-up, costumes and actions of the team are not judged.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the songs with their meaning, written in English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Indian Classical Dance","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Dance Section item i, p.9","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Total performance: 12 to 15 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["The dance is one of these Indian classical dances: Kathak, Kathakali, Bharatnatyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniattam or Odissi.","Up to 3 accompanists. They can include singers, instrumentalists, light curtain operators and similar helpers.","In the Selection Round a sound track or recorded music may be allowed. In the Final Round live accompaniment is compulsory. Live accompaniment is given due credit in the Selection Round."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Classical style dances from films."],"Judging":["Taal, abhinaya or expressions, costumes, footwork, general impression and similar qualities."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of a short note on the dance story in the accompanying song, if any, with its meaning, in Marathi or English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Total performance: 12 to 15 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The dance is one of these Indian classical dances: Kathak, Kathakali, Bharatnatyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniattam or Odissi.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists. They can include singers, instrumentalists, light curtain operators and similar helpers.\\n- In the Selection Round a sound track or recorded music may be allowed. In the Final Round live accompaniment is compulsory. Live accompaniment is given due credit in the Selection Round.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Classical style dances from films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Taal, abhinaya or expressions, costumes, footwork, general impression and similar qualities.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of a short note on the dance story in the accompanying song, if any, with its meaning, in Marathi or English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Indian Folk Dance","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Dance Section item ii, p.9","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Total performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.","The team removes the sets, props and instruments within 2 minutes after the performance."],"Rules":["A single team of 8 to 10 students.","The dance is a primitive Indian tribal dance or a folk dance. It must not be a classical dance.","Live accompaniment is given due credit.","Up to 5 accompanists, back-stage artists and helpers together."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Recorded music.","Dances and folk dances from films."],"Judging":["Originality, authenticity, music, rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of a short note in Marathi or English on the type or style of folk dance and the meaning of the song text, if any, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Total performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 5 minutes at most.\\n- The team removes the sets, props and instruments within 2 minutes after the performance.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 8 to 10 students.\\n- The dance is a primitive Indian tribal dance or a folk dance. It must not be a classical dance.\\n- Live accompaniment is given due credit.\\n- Up to 5 accompanists, back-stage artists and helpers together.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Recorded music.\\n- Dances and folk dances from films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Originality, authenticity, music, rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up and overall effect.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of a short note in Marathi or English on the type or style of folk dance and the meaning of the song text, if any, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Literary Section item i (Elocution Group A, Marathi), p.11","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 4 to 5 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement."],"Rules":["The topic is announced at least one week before the competition.","The language is Marathi.","The speech is in prose, not poetry or song."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Reading from paper."],"Judging":["Introduction, knowledge of the topic, presentation, language style and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 4 to 5 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The topic is announced at least one week before the competition.\\n- The language is Marathi.\\n- The speech is in prose, not poetry or song.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Reading from paper.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Introduction, knowledge of the topic, presentation, language style and overall effect."},{"Title":"Elocution (Any Other Language)","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Literary Section item ii (Elocution Group B, Hindi or English), p.11","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 4 to 5 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement."],"Rules":["The topic is announced at least one week before the competition.","The language is Hindi or English.","The speech is in prose, not poetry or song."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Reading from paper."],"Judging":["Introduction, knowledge of the topic, presentation, language style and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 4 to 5 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The topic is announced at least one week before the competition.\\n- The language is Hindi or English.\\n- The speech is in prose, not poetry or song.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Reading from paper.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Introduction, knowledge of the topic, presentation, language style and overall effect."},{"Title":"Debate","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Literary Section item iii (Debate Group A, Marathi), p.11","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each student speaks for 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Exactly 2 students.","The proposition is announced at least one week before the competition.","The first student speaks FOR the proposition and the second student speaks AGAINST it.","Both students speak in Marathi."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Introduction, knowledge of the topic, presentation, language style and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each student speaks for 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Exactly 2 students.\\n- The proposition is announced at least one week before the competition.\\n- The first student speaks FOR the proposition and the second student speaks AGAINST it.\\n- Both students speak in Marathi.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Introduction, knowledge of the topic, presentation, language style and overall effect."},{"Title":"Debate (Any Other Language)","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Literary Section item iv (Debate Group B, Hindi or English), p.12","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each student speaks for 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Exactly 2 students.","The proposition is announced at least one week before the competition.","The first student speaks FOR the proposition and the second student speaks AGAINST it.","Both students speak in Hindi or English. They may use the same language or different languages, but each student speaks in only one language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Introduction, knowledge of the topic, presentation, language style and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each student speaks for 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Exactly 2 students.\\n- The proposition is announced at least one week before the competition.\\n- The first student speaks FOR the proposition and the second student speaks AGAINST it.\\n- Both students speak in Hindi or English. They may use the same language or different languages, but each student speaks in only one language.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Introduction, knowledge of the topic, presentation, language style and overall effect."},{"Title":"Story Writing","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Literary Section item v (Story Writing Group A, Marathi), p.12","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["The competition lasts 2 hours. The student writes the story under the supervision of officials."],"Rules":["The subject is announced at the time of the competition.","The story is written in Marathi.","The University provides writing sheets. The student brings pen, pencil and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Carrying any written or printed material into the competition."],"Judging":["Introduction, plot, characterization, presentation, relevance, language style and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The competition lasts 2 hours. The student writes the story under the supervision of officials.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The subject is announced at the time of the competition.\\n- The story is written in Marathi.\\n- The University provides writing sheets. The student brings pen, pencil and other materials.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Carrying any written or printed material into the competition.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Introduction, plot, characterization, presentation, relevance, language style and overall effect."},{"Title":"Story Writing (Any Other Language)","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Literary Section item vi (Story Writing Group B, Hindi or English), p.13","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["The competition lasts 2 hours. The student writes the story under the supervision of officials."],"Rules":["The subject is announced at the time of the competition.","The story is written in Hindi or English.","The University provides writing sheets. The student brings pen, pencil and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Carrying any written or printed material into the competition."],"Judging":["Introduction, plot, characterization, presentation, relevance, language style and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The competition lasts 2 hours. The student writes the story under the supervision of officials.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The subject is announced at the time of the competition.\\n- The story is written in Hindi or English.\\n- The University provides writing sheets. The student brings pen, pencil and other materials.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Carrying any written or printed material into the competition.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Introduction, plot, characterization, presentation, relevance, language style and overall effect."},{"Title":"Story Telling","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Literary Section item vii (Story Telling Group A, Marathi), p.13","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement."],"Rules":["The story is authentic, adapted or originally written.","The story is told only in Marathi. The student may use Marathi dialects for the whole story or for some parts or dialogues."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Sensitive subjects such as religious sentiment, stereotyping and politics.","Background music, props and written material during the performance."],"Judging":["Choice of subject, introduction, plot, characterization, presentation, relevance, language style and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of a script of the story are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The story is authentic, adapted or originally written.\\n- The story is told only in Marathi. The student may use Marathi dialects for the whole story or for some parts or dialogues.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Sensitive subjects such as religious sentiment, stereotyping and politics.\\n- Background music, props and written material during the performance.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Choice of subject, introduction, plot, characterization, presentation, relevance, language style and overall effect.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of a script of the story are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Story Telling (Any Other Language)","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Literary Section item viii (Story Telling Group B, Hindi or English), p.14","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement."],"Rules":["The story is authentic, adapted or originally written.","The story is told only in Hindi or English. The student may use Hindi or English dialects for the whole story or for some parts or dialogues."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Sensitive subjects such as religious sentiment, stereotyping and politics.","Background music, props and written material during the performance."],"Judging":["Choice of subject, introduction, plot, characterization, presentation, relevance, language style and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of a script of the story are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The story is authentic, adapted or originally written.\\n- The story is told only in Hindi or English. The student may use Hindi or English dialects for the whole story or for some parts or dialogues.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Sensitive subjects such as religious sentiment, stereotyping and politics.\\n- Background music, props and written material during the performance.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Choice of subject, introduction, plot, characterization, presentation, relevance, language style and overall effect.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of a script of the story are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Quiz","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Literary Section item ix, p.14","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["A single team of 3 students.","The quiz has two rounds: the Zonal/District Level Cultural Youth Festival (Selection Round) and the University Level Cultural Youth Festival (Final Round).","In the Selection Round the team writes answers to objective questions. All questions are in English only. The time for writing the answers is 15 minutes.","At most 6 teams are chosen on merit from the Preliminary Round for the Final Round.","The Final Round is oral, in an audio-visual format.","The referee announces the specific rules for the Final Round, the evaluation system, the time to replay a question and the type of rounds before the competition starts."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 3 students.\\n- The quiz has two rounds: the Zonal/District Level Cultural Youth Festival (Selection Round) and the University Level Cultural Youth Festival (Final Round).\\n- In the Selection Round the team writes answers to objective questions. All questions are in English only. The time for writing the answers is 15 minutes.\\n- At most 6 teams are chosen on merit from the Preliminary Round for the Final Round.\\n- The Final Round is oral, in an audio-visual format.\\n- The referee announces the specific rules for the Final Round, the evaluation system, the time to replay a question and the type of rounds before the competition starts."},{"Title":"Mono Acting","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Theatre Section item i (Mono Acting Group A, Marathi), p.15","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement."],"Rules":["The student acts in Marathi only."],"Allowed":["Costumes and make-up. Only acting skills are judged."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Theme, acting, general impression and similar qualities."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student acts in Marathi only.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Costumes and make-up. Only acting skills are judged.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Theme, acting, general impression and similar qualities.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Mono Acting (Any Other Language)","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Theatre Section item ii (Mono Acting Group C, other than Marathi), p.15","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement."],"Rules":["The student acts in any regional or official language of India other than Marathi."],"Allowed":["Costumes and make-up. Only acting skills are judged."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Theme, acting, general impression and similar qualities."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 5 to 7 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student acts in any regional or official language of India other than Marathi.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Costumes and make-up. Only acting skills are judged.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Theme, acting, general impression and similar qualities.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Mimicry","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Theatre Section item iii, p.16","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 4 to 5 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement."],"Rules":["The student may mimic the sound of machines, characters and speeches of well-known personalities, and similar items.","The student presents the mimicry in any regional or official language of India, or in English."],"Allowed":["Naming the character on the stage."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Skill of imitation, variety of sounds and voices, and presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the list of characters to be imitated, written in Marathi, Hindi or English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 4 to 5 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student may mimic the sound of machines, characters and speeches of well-known personalities, and similar items.\\n- The student presents the mimicry in any regional or official language of India, or in English.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Naming the character on the stage.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Skill of imitation, variety of sounds and voices, and presentation.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the list of characters to be imitated, written in Marathi, Hindi or English, are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"One Act Play","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Theatre Section item iv (One Act Play Group A, Marathi), p.16","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 25 to 30 minutes. Time counting starts when the announcement starts or the curtain is fully open, whichever is earlier.","Making the arrangement for the set and light: 10 minutes before the play. Taking it down: 5 minutes after the play."],"Rules":["A single team of 2 to 9 students.","The play is in prose or in verse, in Marathi only.","The College, Institute or University Academic Department alone is responsible for having the script censored, and for all permissions and censor certificates.","The same institution cannot repeat a play in consecutive Youth Festivals.","The University normally provides five spot lights and general make-up facilities, where available. Extra lights, set, props and special make-up are arranged by the institution at its own cost and risk.","Up to 3 accompanists, back-stage artists, workers and helpers together."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Box sets."],"Judging":["Theme, acting, direction, general impression and similar qualities of the play."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 25 to 30 minutes. Time counting starts when the announcement starts or the curtain is fully open, whichever is earlier.\\n- Making the arrangement for the set and light: 10 minutes before the play. Taking it down: 5 minutes after the play.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 2 to 9 students.\\n- The play is in prose or in verse, in Marathi only.\\n- The College, Institute or University Academic Department alone is responsible for having the script censored, and for all permissions and censor certificates.\\n- The same institution cannot repeat a play in consecutive Youth Festivals.\\n- The University normally provides five spot lights and general make-up facilities, where available. Extra lights, set, props and special make-up are arranged by the institution at its own cost and risk.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists, back-stage artists, workers and helpers together.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Box sets.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Theme, acting, direction, general impression and similar qualities of the play.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"One Act Play (Any Other Language)","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Theatre Section item v (One-Act-Play Group C, other than Marathi), p.17","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 25 to 30 minutes. Time counting starts when the announcement starts or the curtain is fully open, whichever is earlier.","Making the arrangement for the set and light: 10 minutes before the play. Taking it down: 5 minutes after the play."],"Rules":["A single team of 2 to 9 students.","The play is in prose or in verse, in any regional or official language of India other than Marathi.","The College, Institute or University Academic Department alone is responsible for having the script censored, and for all permissions and censor certificates.","The same institution cannot repeat a play in consecutive Youth Festivals.","The University normally provides five spot lights and general make-up facilities, where available. Extra lights, set, props and special make-up are arranged by the institution at its own cost and risk.","Up to 3 accompanists, back-stage artists, workers and helpers together."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Box sets."],"Judging":["Theme, acting, direction, general impression and similar qualities of the play."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 25 to 30 minutes. Time counting starts when the announcement starts or the curtain is fully open, whichever is earlier.\\n- Making the arrangement for the set and light: 10 minutes before the play. Taking it down: 5 minutes after the play.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 2 to 9 students.\\n- The play is in prose or in verse, in any regional or official language of India other than Marathi.\\n- The College, Institute or University Academic Department alone is responsible for having the script censored, and for all permissions and censor certificates.\\n- The same institution cannot repeat a play in consecutive Youth Festivals.\\n- The University normally provides five spot lights and general make-up facilities, where available. Extra lights, set, props and special make-up are arranged by the institution at its own cost and risk.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists, back-stage artists, workers and helpers together.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Box sets.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Theme, acting, direction, general impression and similar qualities of the play.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Skit","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Theatre Section item vi (Skit Group A, Marathi), p.18","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts when the announcement starts or the curtain is fully open, whichever is earlier.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["A single team of 4 to 6 students.","The skit is in Marathi only.","The skit should preferably highlight a theme of national or social importance.","The skit must keep an acceptable level of decency. If it does not, the item is disqualified.","Only innocent satire or humour is expected.","The same institution cannot repeat a skit in consecutive Youth Festivals.","Up to 3 accompanists, back-stage artists, workers and helpers together."],"Allowed":["Make-up, drapery and background music."],"NotAllowed":["Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination.","Vulgarity or bitter insinuations in the presentation."],"Judging":["Theme, acting, co-ordination, general impression and similar qualities."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts when the announcement starts or the curtain is fully open, whichever is earlier.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 4 to 6 students.\\n- The skit is in Marathi only.\\n- The skit should preferably highlight a theme of national or social importance.\\n- The skit must keep an acceptable level of decency. If it does not, the item is disqualified.\\n- Only innocent satire or humour is expected.\\n- The same institution cannot repeat a skit in consecutive Youth Festivals.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists, back-stage artists, workers and helpers together.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Make-up, drapery and background music.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination.\\n- Vulgarity or bitter insinuations in the presentation.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Theme, acting, co-ordination, general impression and similar qualities.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Skit (Any Other Language)","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Theatre Section item vii (Skit Group C, other than Marathi), p.18","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts when the announcement starts or the curtain is fully open, whichever is earlier.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["A single team of 4 to 6 students.","The skit is in any regional or official language of India other than Marathi.","The skit should preferably highlight a theme of national or social importance.","The skit must keep an acceptable level of decency. If it does not, the item is disqualified.","Only innocent satire or humour is expected.","The same institution cannot repeat a skit in consecutive Youth Festivals.","Up to 3 accompanists, back-stage artists, workers and helpers together."],"Allowed":["Make-up, drapery and background music."],"NotAllowed":["Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination.","Vulgarity or bitter insinuations in the presentation."],"Judging":["Theme, acting, co-ordination, general impression and similar qualities."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 8 to 10 minutes. Time counting starts when the announcement starts or the curtain is fully open, whichever is earlier.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 4 to 6 students.\\n- The skit is in any regional or official language of India other than Marathi.\\n- The skit should preferably highlight a theme of national or social importance.\\n- The skit must keep an acceptable level of decency. If it does not, the item is disqualified.\\n- Only innocent satire or humour is expected.\\n- The same institution cannot repeat a skit in consecutive Youth Festivals.\\n- Up to 3 accompanists, back-stage artists, workers and helpers together.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Make-up, drapery and background music.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination.\\n- Vulgarity or bitter insinuations in the presentation.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Theme, acting, co-ordination, general impression and similar qualities.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Three copies of the script, three copies of the theme of the script explained in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of the printed Form of Role Played are handed in at registration on the day of the competition."},{"Title":"Mime","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Theatre Section item viii, p.19","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performance: 4 to 5 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.","Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most."],"Rules":["A single team of 4 to 6 students.","The students wear white or black skin-tight dresses and paint their faces with raised eyebrows and broadened lips.","The idea is shown only through expressions and gestures.","The University normally provides general make-up facilities, where available.","Up to 2 accompanists and back-stage artists together."],"Allowed":["Music, to strengthen the performance."],"NotAllowed":["Any property."],"Judging":["The idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performance: 4 to 5 minutes. Time counting starts right after the organisers' final announcement.\\n- Stage and instrument setting: 3 minutes at most.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 4 to 6 students.\\n- The students wear white or black skin-tight dresses and paint their faces with raised eyebrows and broadened lips.\\n- The idea is shown only through expressions and gestures.\\n- The University normally provides general make-up facilities, where available.\\n- Up to 2 accompanists and back-stage artists together.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Music, to strengthen the performance.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Any property.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up and general impression."},{"Title":"On the Spot Painting","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Fine Art Section item i, p.20","Sections":{"About":["Individual event, held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the painting: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The student paints on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.","The paper is half imperial size drawing paper (22 inches long and 15 inches wide). The University provides the paper.","The painting is done in water colours, poster colours or pastel colours.","The student brings brushes, paints and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Visualization, delivery of the subject, composition, colour application, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event, held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the painting: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student paints on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.\\n- The paper is half imperial size drawing paper (22 inches long and 15 inches wide). The University provides the paper.\\n- The painting is done in water colours, poster colours or pastel colours.\\n- The student brings brushes, paints and other materials.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Visualization, delivery of the subject, composition, colour application, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Collage","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Fine Art Section item ii, p.20","Sections":{"About":["Individual event, held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the collage: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The student makes the collage on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.","The paper is half imperial size mount board paper (22 inches long and 15 inches wide). The University provides it.","The collage is made from old magazines. The University provides the old magazines.","The student brings pasting material and other materials needed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, composition, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event, held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the collage: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student makes the collage on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.\\n- The paper is half imperial size mount board paper (22 inches long and 15 inches wide). The University provides it.\\n- The collage is made from old magazines. The University provides the old magazines.\\n- The student brings pasting material and other materials needed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, composition, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Poster Making","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Fine Art Section item iii, p.21","Sections":{"About":["Individual event, held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the poster: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The student makes the poster on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.","The paper is half imperial size mount board paper (22 inches long by 15 inches wide). The University provides it.","The poster is done in water colours, poster colours or pastel colours.","The student brings brushes, paints and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Visualization, delivery of the subject, presentation, tagline and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event, held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the poster: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student makes the poster on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.\\n- The paper is half imperial size mount board paper (22 inches long by 15 inches wide). The University provides it.\\n- The poster is done in water colours, poster colours or pastel colours.\\n- The student brings brushes, paints and other materials.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Visualization, delivery of the subject, presentation, tagline and overall impact."},{"Title":"Clay Modeling","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Fine Art Section item iv, p.21","Sections":{"About":["Individual event, held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the clay work: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The student makes the clay work on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.","The University provides the clay.","The student brings his or her own material for making the clay work."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, composition, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event, held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the clay work: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student makes the clay work on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.\\n- The University provides the clay.\\n- The student brings his or her own material for making the clay work.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, composition, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Cartooning","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Fine Art Section item v, p.21","Sections":{"About":["Individual event, held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the cartoon: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The student makes the cartoon on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.","The paper is half imperial size drawing paper (22 inches long by 15 inches wide). The University provides it.","The student brings brushes, paints and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Visualization, delivery of the subject, characters, synchronization, colour application, composition, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event, held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the cartoon: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student makes the cartoon on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.\\n- The paper is half imperial size drawing paper (22 inches long by 15 inches wide). The University provides it.\\n- The student brings brushes, paints and other materials.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Visualization, delivery of the subject, characters, synchronization, colour application, composition, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Rangoli","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Fine Art Section item vi, p.22","Sections":{"About":["Individual event, held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the rangoli: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The student makes the rangoli on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.","The student gets a space of 120 cm by 120 cm.","The student uses only rangoli powder and coloured powders.","The student brings white rangoli powder and the other material needed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Any reference such as a greeting or a printed material or picture in miniature form."],"Judging":["Visualization, delivery of the subject, colour scheme, elements, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event, held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the rangoli: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student makes the rangoli on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.\\n- The student gets a space of 120 cm by 120 cm.\\n- The student uses only rangoli powder and coloured powders.\\n- The student brings white rangoli powder and the other material needed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Any reference such as a greeting or a printed material or picture in miniature form.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Visualization, delivery of the subject, colour scheme, elements, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Mehendi Designing","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Fine Art Section item vii, p.22","Sections":{"About":["Individual event, held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the mehendi: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The student makes the mehendi design on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.","The student draws the mehendi on the palm side of both hands of a model. The model is a student of the same institution.","The mehendi extends to the palm side of the forearm for at least six inches.","The student brings the mehendi and the other material needed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Hand prints, any kind of mould and decorative material."],"Judging":["Originality, creativity, decorative art with aesthetic sense, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event, held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the mehendi: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student makes the mehendi design on the subject given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.\\n- The student draws the mehendi on the palm side of both hands of a model. The model is a student of the same institution.\\n- The mehendi extends to the palm side of the forearm for at least six inches.\\n- The student brings the mehendi and the other material needed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Hand prints, any kind of mould and decorative material.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Originality, creativity, decorative art with aesthetic sense, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Spot Photography","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Fine Art Section item viii, p.23","Sections":{"About":["Individual event, held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the photography: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The student submits only the 5 best photographs on the subject, topic or theme given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.","The student brings his or her own digital camera.","The camera has a memory card. The judges format the memory card before the competition starts.","The University keeps the right to use the photographs submitted by the student when it needs to.","Extra instructions are announced when the competition starts."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Mixing, matching or morphing of photographs.","Software such as Photoshop or Picasa to improve the images."],"Judging":["Impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event, held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the photography: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The student submits only the 5 best photographs on the subject, topic or theme given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.\\n- The student brings his or her own digital camera.\\n- The camera has a memory card. The judges format the memory card before the competition starts.\\n- The University keeps the right to use the photographs submitted by the student when it needs to.\\n- Extra instructions are announced when the competition starts.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Mixing, matching or morphing of photographs.\\n- Software such as Photoshop or Picasa to improve the images.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."},{"Title":"Installation","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Fine Art Section item ix, p.23","Sections":{"About":["Group event, held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish the installation: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["A single team of 3 to 4 students.","The team installs or creates an atmosphere related to the subject, title or theme given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.","The team makes only one installation, not bigger than 5 feet by 5 feet by 5 feet.","The team may use all the materials used in other art events such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modelling.","The team may use waste material found around, or any material from outside.","The team makes its own image or form from raw material."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Ready-made images or forms available in the market."],"Judging":["Visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, synchronization, composition, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event, held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time to finish the installation: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A single team of 3 to 4 students.\\n- The team installs or creates an atmosphere related to the subject, title or theme given by the panel of judges at the time of the competition.\\n- The team makes only one installation, not bigger than 5 feet by 5 feet by 5 feet.\\n- The team may use all the materials used in other art events such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modelling.\\n- The team may use waste material found around, or any material from outside.\\n- The team makes its own image or form from raw material.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Ready-made images or forms available in the market.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, synchronization, composition, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Short Film Making","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Short Film Making, p.25","Sections":{"About":["Group event."],"TimeAndFormat":["The film is not more than 5 minutes long, including the beginning and end credits. A longer film can be rejected.","The film is at least 30 seconds long, including credits."],"Rules":["Each institution submits a single short film, on any subject or theme.","The institution's students perform all lead and side roles. There is no limit on the number of students.","Students may do the direction, script, dialogue writing, lyrics, music direction, camera, light, art direction, editing and similar work, or they may invite other persons. Due credit is given if students did this work.","The students show the final film to the Principal of the College, Director of the Institute or Head of the Department. They submit a letter from that person to the Director, Department of Students' Development, University of Mumbai, approving the content of the film, when they submit the film.","The film is shot or completed after {{FilmCompletedAfterDate}}.","The film can be in any regional or official language of India. It must have English subtitles when it is in a language other than Marathi or Hindi.","The film can be shot in MPEG4 or AVI format. The recommended ratios are 16:9 and 16:9 Full Height Anamorphic, in DV or HDV.","The University keeps non-exclusive rights to screen the film at any level and to show it for non-commercial purposes. It also keeps the right to send the film to any national or international film festival or competition.","The University is not responsible for any unauthorised use of the content by a third party. It does not promise to post any content.","A film selected and submitted for the final screening cannot be withdrawn under any circumstances."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Documentaries. The competition is based on the concept of a film.","Content, dialogues, lyrics or music that hurt the feelings of any person, society, religion and so on.","A film that was submitted to any other competition or festival before. If this is found later, the film is disqualified or the prize is withheld."],"Judging":["Content originality (quality of storyline and script), production (camera work, lighting and shot composition), post-production (editing, transitions, pacing, continuity and flow), image (focus, colour and lighting) and sound quality (clarity, consistency of audio levels and lack of noise)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Group event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The film is not more than 5 minutes long, including the beginning and end credits. A longer film can be rejected.\\n- The film is at least 30 seconds long, including credits.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institution submits a single short film, on any subject or theme.\\n- The institution's students perform all lead and side roles. There is no limit on the number of students.\\n- Students may do the direction, script, dialogue writing, lyrics, music direction, camera, light, art direction, editing and similar work, or they may invite other persons. Due credit is given if students did this work.\\n- The students show the final film to the Principal of the College, Director of the Institute or Head of the Department. They submit a letter from that person to the Director, Department of Students' Development, University of Mumbai, approving the content of the film, when they submit the film.\\n- The film is shot or completed after {{FilmCompletedAfterDate}}.\\n- The film can be in any regional or official language of India. It must have English subtitles when it is in a language other than Marathi or Hindi.\\n- The film can be shot in MPEG4 or AVI format. The recommended ratios are 16:9 and 16:9 Full Height Anamorphic, in DV or HDV.\\n- The University keeps non-exclusive rights to screen the film at any level and to show it for non-commercial purposes. It also keeps the right to send the film to any national or international film festival or competition.\\n- The University is not responsible for any unauthorised use of the content by a third party. It does not promise to post any content.\\n- A film selected and submitted for the final screening cannot be withdrawn under any circumstances.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Documentaries. The competition is based on the concept of a film.\\n- Content, dialogues, lyrics or music that hurt the feelings of any person, society, religion and so on.\\n- A film that was submitted to any other competition or festival before. If this is found later, the film is disqualified or the prize is withheld.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Content originality (quality of storyline and script), production (camera work, lighting and shot composition), post-production (editing, transitions, pacing, continuity and flow), image (focus, colour and lighting) and sound quality (clarity, consistency of audio levels and lack of noise)."},{"Title":"Jackpot","Source":"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Jackpot, p.27","Sections":{"About":["Individual event."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Each institution sends 1 boy and 1 girl student co-ordinator. A Women's College sends 2 girl students.","Only the student co-ordinators of the institution's contingent can take part.","The student participants attend the meeting of student co-ordinators that the University announces from time to time."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The student participants are judged on these components: Personality Contest, Cultural Performance, Physical Endurance or Skill, Intelligence Quotient (IQ) and General Awareness, Oratory (public speaking or compering), Leadership, Academic Performance, Assessment of Profile, Medical Fitness and Psychological Testing."],"Points":["The maximum marks in each component are 10. They are converted to a ten point scale after dividing by ten."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Individual event.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institution sends 1 boy and 1 girl student co-ordinator. A Women's College sends 2 girl students.\\n- Only the student co-ordinators of the institution's contingent can take part.\\n- The student participants attend the meeting of student co-ordinators that the University announces from time to time.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The student participants are judged on these components: Personality Contest, Cultural Performance, Physical Endurance or Skill, Intelligence Quotient (IQ) and General Awareness, Oratory (public speaking or compering), Leadership, Academic Performance, Assessment of Profile, Medical Fitness and Psychological Testing.\\n\\n## Points\\n- The maximum marks in each component are 10. They are converted to a ten point scale after dividing by ten."}]`),s=[],r=[{Key:"FestivalEdition",Kind:"text",Label:"Festival and academic year",Value:"57th Inter-Collegiate / Institute / Department Youth Festival, Academic Year 2024-25",Source:"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, p.1"},{Key:"AgeCutoffDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date on which age is counted (students must be under 25)",Value:"2024-09-30",Source:"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Eligibility rules, p.1-2 (B)(b): under 25 years of age as on September 30, 2024"},{Key:"FilmCompletedAfterDate",Kind:"date",Label:"A short film must be shot or completed after this date",Value:"2022-07-31",Source:"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, Short Film Making, p.25"},{Key:"Organiser",Kind:"text",Label:"Organiser",Value:"Department of Students' Development, University of Mumbai",Source:"University of Mumbai 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 Rules, p.1-3 (page header)"}],l=[{Claim:"Eligibility rules (A General, B Eligibility with explanation, C Disqualification) and all event rules for the Music, Dance, Literary, Theatre and Fine Art sections, Short Film Making and Jackpot are taken from the University's own 2024-25 rules circular.",SourceType:"Primary - University of Mumbai, Department of Students' Development official 'Rules and Regulations of the 57th Inter-Collegiate/Institute/Department Youth Festival, Academic Year 2024-25'",Source:"Rules and Regulations of the 57th Youth Festival 2024-25 (27 pages)",Url:"https://unimumbaidsd.com/2024-25/docs/Circular-Rules-YF-2024-25.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2024,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:i,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:a,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{o as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,a as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,i as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,h as Year,u as default};
